.TH "PB-ENV-TEAM" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-team - Manage encrypted ENV team scopes


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env team [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage encrypted ENV team scopes

.PP
Create team ENV scopes, grant access, rotate keys, revoke members, or reset values. These operations affect encrypted team custody rather than ordinary team membership alone.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for team


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-team-create(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-team-grant(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-team-reset(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-team-revoke(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-team-rotate(1)\fP
